It just came to my mind that there is a sword in the Norse legends
that might make an interesting new artifact for nethack: Tirfing (or
Tyrfing, whichever spelling you prefer).

In the legends Tirfing was forged by dwarves and it could cleave a
rock in two. However, since the smith was forced to forge it, he
laid a heavy curse on it: once drawn it couldn't be sheated before it
killed someone and it would destroy all its owners in the end.

So, in nethack terms it would be a (broad or long) sword that:

 - intelligent chaotic
 - ignores enemy AC
 - doubles damage (or something else, heavy damage bonus in any case)
 - autocurses when wielded
 - autouncurses after some monster is killed with it.

The "destroys owners" part could be implemented, for example, as a
summon nasties spell that triggers with random interval depending on 
the character level: the higher the level, the more often will it
happen. Of course, a really high level character doesn't have to worry
about nasties anymore, so it might be prudent to throw in some
archons, too.

